---
import ProjectPageLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectPageLayout.astro';
import SpecTable from '../../components/SpecTable.astro';
import MetricCallout from '../../components/MetricCallout.astro';
import PdfViewer from '../../components/PdfViewer.astro';

const specRows = [
  { label: 'Course',    value: 'Engr. 1, Intro. to Rocketry (E1RK)'                    },
  { label: 'Mentors',   value: 'Nicholas Veracruz (SpaceX, Relativity) · Caitlyn Hill (SpaceX)' },
  { label: 'Design',    value: 'SolidWorks · OpenRocket · Theodore von Kármán'         },
  { label: 'Build',     value: 'FDM 3D Print'                                           },
  { label: 'Material',  value: 'Polylactic Acid (PLA)'                                  },
  { label: 'Color',     value: 'Grass Green'                                            },
];
---
<ProjectPageLayout
  title="3D Printed Rocket"
  description="FDM-fabricated sounding rocket designed in OpenRocket and SolidWorks for UCLA's E1RK course."
  ghostText="E1RK 3DPR"
  category="E1RK — UCLA"
  tagline="FDM sounding rocket — OpenRocket design + SolidWorks CAD"
  showOverview={false}
  nextHref="/projects/group-high-powered-rocket"
>
  <!-- Overview + launch video on right (16:9 landscape) -->
  <section class="spec-block" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; align-items: start; gap: 1.5rem;">
    <div class="spec-col">
      <h2 class="section-overview">Overview</h2>
      <SpecTable rows={specRows} title="Specifications" />
    </div>
    <div class="launch-wrap">
      <video class="launch-video" autoplay loop muted playsinline
             aria-label="3D printed rocket launch footage">
        <source src="/assets/projects/3dpr/launch_video.MP4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="metrics-row" aria-label="Key metrics">
    <MetricCallout value="20.2" unit="g"   description="Fuselage weight"      />
    <MetricCallout value="???"  unit="ft"  description="Apogee"               />
    <MetricCallout value="12"   unit="in"  description="Height"               />
  </section>

  <section class="the-work">
    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Constraints</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <p class="work-text">
          Engineered to a tight flight envelope: under 3 oz with the Estes A8-3 motor, 1.10 to 2.50 calibers of static stability, at least 15.24 m/s rail-exit velocity, under 5 m/s descent, and a fully 3D-printed PLA airframe with parachute recovery and at least 15 cm^3 of chute space.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Approach</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <p class="work-text">
          Designed a freeform three-fin airframe in SolidWorks with an elliptical nosecone and Starship-inspired nose fins, then validated static stability and flight performance in OpenRocket against the 1.10 to 2.50 caliber target.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Build</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <p class="work-text">
          Led build of the all-PLA airframe, printing four body-tube iterations to converge on the thinnest structurally viable wall and minimize mass against the under-3 oz limit, plus three nosecone iterations to resolve nose-fin printability at small scale.
        </p>
        <!-- 3d_print (portrait 3:4) + prototype_B (portrait 3:4) — side by side -->
        <div class="proj-gallery proj-gallery--2">
          <figure class="proj-figure">
            <img src="/assets/projects/3dpr/3d_print.jpg"
                 alt="First layer of 3D print on Bambu Lab P1S" loading="lazy"
                 style="aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover;" />
            <figcaption>First layer of 3D print on Bambu Lab P1S</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="proj-figure">
            <img src="/assets/projects/3dpr/prototype_B.jpg"
                 alt="3D printed rocket prototype" loading="lazy"
                 style="aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover;" />
          </figure>
        </div>
        <!-- fins (4:3) + nose_cone (4:3) — side by side -->
        <div class="proj-gallery proj-gallery--2">
          <figure class="proj-figure">
            <img src="/assets/projects/3dpr/fins.jpg"
                 alt="Printed rocket fins" loading="lazy" />
          </figure>
          <figure class="proj-figure">
            <img src="/assets/projects/3dpr/nose_cone.jpg"
                 alt="3D printed nose cone" loading="lazy" />
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Analysis</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <p class="work-text">
          The internal shock-cord ring cut into parachute space. Verified in OpenRocket that total mass held under 3 oz and rail-exit velocity stayed above 15.24 m/s.
        </p>
        <figure class="proj-figure">
          <img src="/assets/projects/3dpr/body_weight.jpg"
               alt="Weighing rocket components for OpenRocket simulation input" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Weights of components were plugged into OpenRocket simulations to streamline the design loop</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Design Review</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <!-- Design review slide deck — 7 pages, arrow-navigable -->
        <PdfViewer
          src="/assets/projects/3dpr/review_slides.pdf"
          pages={7}
          label="3DPR design review slides"
          aspectRatio="16 / 9"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Result</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <p class="work-text">
          Achieved a near-vertical boost with only a slight launch-rail angle; the parachute failed to deploy, but the shock-cord held, and the airframe survived.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-row">
      <h2 class="work-label">Reflection</h2>
      <div class="work-content">
        <p class="work-text">
          With airframe/stability proven in flight, the recovery failure taught me a valuable lesson. I'd improve our recovery system design, as the constrained parachute space most likely drove the non-deployment.
        </p>
        <figure class="proj-figure">
          <img src="/assets/projects/3dpr/team_picture.JPG"
               alt="E1RK team photo" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProjectPageLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Launch video — 16:9 in spec-block ──────────────── */
  .launch-wrap {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .launch-video {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .spec-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .spec-col :global(.section-overview) {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: var(--fw-black);
    color: var(--text-100);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Scramble the "???" apogee counter
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    const CHARS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789!@#';
    const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.metric__value[data-target="???"]');
    if (!el) return;

    let frame = 0;
    const FRAMES = 24;

    const timer = setInterval(() => {
      frame++;
      el.textContent = '???'
        .split('')
        .map(() => CHARS[Math.floor(Math.random() * CHARS.length)])
        .join('');
      if (frame >= FRAMES) {
        el.textContent = '???';
        clearInterval(timer);
      }
    }, 60);
  });
</script>
